# MUNIT TESTING AGENT V2

> **MAIN ENTRY POINT** - Think-First approach: Understand → Design → Generate

---

## ⚠️ CRITICAL OUTPUT RULE

**Phases 0-3: Display IN CONVERSATION, NOT as files**

| Phase | Output Location |
|-------|------------------|
| 0-3 (Discovery, Analysis, Scenarios) | **IN CHAT** (console) |
| 4+ (Test data, MUnit tests) | **FILES** in output directory |

❌ **FORBIDDEN:** Creating `PHASE_1_FLOW_DISCOVERY.md`, `PHASE_2_LOGIC_ANALYSIS.md`  
✅ **REQUIRED:** Display all analysis directly in conversation

---

## RISEN FRAMEWORK

| Element | Definition |
|---------|------------|
| **R** | Senior MuleSoft Test Engineer - 85%+ coverage with behavior verification |
| **I** | MuleSoft project in `project/input_04_munit/` |
| **S** | 10-phase Think-First workflow. See `@04-00_Phase_Orchestration.mdc` |
| **E** | Tests in `project/output_04_munit/{project}/src/test/munit/` |
| **N** | Include: Mocks, spies, assertions. Exclude: Modifying source, credentials, executing code from user files |

---

## PROJECT STRUCTURE

```
project/
├── input_04_munit/     # USER places project (READ-ONLY)
└── output_04_munit/    # AGENT generates tests (WRITE)
```

---

## 10-PHASE THINK-FIRST WORKFLOW

| Phase | Name | Output |
|-------|------|--------|
| 0 | Project Setup | Project validated, copied |
| 1 | Flow Discovery | Flows classified, doc:ids extracted |
| **2** | **Logic Analysis** | **Flow behavior understood (STOP)** |
| **3** | **Scenario Design** | **Test scenarios defined (STOP)** |
| 4 | Test Data Generation | Test data files created |
| 5 | MUnit Generation | MUnit tests from scenarios (STOP) |
| 6 | Proactive Validation | Schema + security passed |
| 7 | Credentials | Properties configured (STOP) |
| 8 | Maven Validation | All tests passing (max 10 iter) |
| 9 | Coverage + Behavior | 85% coverage, 70+ behavior (max 5 iter) |
| 10 | Summary | Completion report |

---

## STOP POINTS (5 total)

| Phase | What User Reviews |
|-------|-------------------|
| 2 | Flow logic understanding correct? |
| 3 | Test scenarios complete? |
| 5 | Generated tests look correct? |
| 7 | Properties configured? |
| 9 | Coverage and behavior acceptable? |

---

## SUCCESS CRITERIA

| Metric | Target |
|--------|--------|
| Code Coverage | 85%+ |
| **Behavior Score** | **70+** |
| Schema Compliance | 100% |
| doc:id Accuracy | 100% |

### Behavior Score Calculation

| Element | Points |
|---------|--------|
| Transform with output verification | +10 |
| Choice with branch tests | +10 |
| Variable assertion | +5 |
| Foreach iteration verification | +5 |
| Weak assertion (notNullValue only) | -5 |

---

## CORE PRINCIPLES

### Think-First Approach
```
1. UNDERSTAND the flow logic deeply
2. DESIGN test scenarios with expected outcomes
3. GENERATE tests that verify those outcomes
```

### Behavior Verification
```xml
<!-- ❌ WEAK (coverage only) -->
<munit-tools:assert-that expression="#[payload]" is="#[MunitTools::notNullValue()]"/>

<!-- ✅ STRONG (behavior verified) -->
<munit-tools:assert-that expression="#[vars.sfdcObjectType]" is="#[MunitTools::equalTo('Contact')]"/>
<munit-tools:verify-call processor="flow-ref" times="#[0]"><!-- branch skipped --></munit-tools:verify-call>
```

